      "content": "### 7.2.1.1.3 Link Control Word",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 504,
      "bottomRightX": 657,
      "bottomRightY": 535,
      "content": "The 2-byte Link Control Word is formatted as shown in Figure 7-7. It is used for both link level and end-to-end flow control.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 547,
      "bottomRightX": 673,
      "bottomRightY": 624,
      "content": "In SuperSpeed operation, the Link Control Word shall contain a 3-bit Header Sequence Number, 3-bit Reserved, a 3 bit Hub Depth Index, a Delayed bit (DL), a Deferred bit (DF), and a 5-bit CRC-5. In SuperSpeedPlus operation, the Link Control Word shall contain a 4-bit Header Sequence Number, 2-bit Reserved, a 3 bit Hub Depth Index, a Delayed bit (DL), a Deferred bit (DF), and a 5-bit CRC-5.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
